From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Niklas Sheth <hi@niklassheth.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 12:39:30 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: G16: Hang reports name processes and
 slot/Work-memory reuse

Capture the submitting tgid at ioctl time in the render and compute
parameters (submission can be retried from a worker) and print it on
every hang flight line and ring entry. Ring headers also carry the VM
root, the framebuffer size from 3D register 0x15211 and the TA/3D
stamps. The recent ring is printed whole in the hang report, so it
shows everything submitted on the GPU just before a stuck render.

Folded in:
- WIP drm/asahi: G16 hang reports name each flight's process; full recent ring
- WIP drm/asahi: G16 hang reports name processes and slot/Work-memory reuse

[WIP drm/asahi: G16 hang reports name processes and slot/Work-memory reuse]
Capture the submitter's comm with its tgid and print it on hang flight
lines and ring entries, since clients are often gone by the time a hang
is analysed. Keep a 256-entry log of retired Works (slot, VM, process,
ordinal, submit and retire times; capacity reserved at Work allocation
so retirement never allocates) and each slot's latest rebinding. For
every stuck render the hang report now says when its slot last changed
VMs, when the previous occupant's last Work there retired relative to
the rebind and the stuck submit, and who used the stuck Work's memory
before it and when that Work retired. Ring entries also carry their
submission time (CLOCK_MONOTONIC, comparable with dmesg), and the rings
print the time of the hang report.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
